<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Witu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Witu is a town in Lamu County on the coast of Kenya, north-west of Lamu Island. It became the fortified capital of the sultanate of Witu, founded around 1860 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-simba">Ahmad Simba</a> of the Nabhani family after he fled the forces of Zanzibar. In 1885 it became the centre of a German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, and in 1890 a British expedition sacked the town after Germans had been killed there.</p></div>
